{
  "id": "52073c33-5f7d-479b-b2db-238c6e280c9a",
  "slug": "3sum-exponent",
  "name": "3SUM Exponent",
  "description": "Classical algorithms solve 3SUM in $O(n^2)$ time. In a 2026 breakthrough, [Alman and Vassilevska Williams](https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1) gave a deterministic $O(n^{1.9992})$ algorithm, refuting the integer 3SUM hypothesis. How low can the exponent go?\n\nBuilding on existing Lean formalizations, this campaign tracks upper bounds for 3SUM on polynomially bounded integers, using a word RAM with $O(\\log n)$-bit words, and pursues smaller exponents.",
  "template_proposal_id": "35734a46-dd9b-4a8d-8e6e-cea1cd2c855f",
  "foundation_mission_id": "487064c8-0ffb-4779-802b-6824b289a73c",
  "env": {
    "mathlib_rev": "0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474",
